# Generated by stop-bots {VERSION}, with `stop-bots install cron`.
# stop-bots-template: {SHA256}
#
# Re-running that command replaces this file for as long as it is
# unedited: the stop-bots-template line is a hash of everything else
# here, and is how it tells. An edited copy is left alone, and the
# installer says so; `--force` replaces it anyway.
#
# Once a minute, run whatever is due on stop-bots' schedule: the same
# jobs the TUI runs while it is open, which `stop-bots status` and the
# TUI's Dashboard show. It writes what the detectors find, and applies
# it to the web server and the firewall only as far as
# `set-auto-apply` and `set-auto-apply-firewall` allow -- both are off
# until you turn them on.
SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
* * * * * root /usr/bin/stop-bots tick --db /var/lib/stop-bots/db.sqlite3
